adjudication.rationale:
In packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts, the cancel flow now attempts to resolve a calendar credential by id from the database when it is not found under bookingToDelete.user.credentials:

```ts
let calendarCredential = bookingToDelete.user.credentials.find((c) => c.id === credentialId);
if (!calendarCredential) {
  const foundCalendarCredential = await prisma.credential.findUnique({ where: { id: credentialId } });
  if (foundCalendarCredential) calendarCredential = foundCalendarCredential;
}
```

This removes the prior ownership restriction (only acting on the booking user's credentials). If a booking reference contains a stale/mismatched credentialId, the code will act on whatever credential exists with that id, without verifying it belongs to bookingToDelete.user (e.g., matching userId/teamId). That can lead to deleting/updating calendar events using a credential not owned by the booking’s user (correctness and potential authorization issue).
